# Same-origin proxies back to the Django backend.
#
# The browser must never talk to the backend host directly: a public page
# (rtutindahan.netlify.app) that fetches a tailnet address is blocked by
# Chrome's Private Network Access rules, and the backend hostname changes
# whenever the tunnel is re-minted. Proxying through Netlify's edge keeps the
# API, the Django admin and its static files on this site's own origin.
#
# Upstream = the Cloudflare quick tunnel for kallisto-1:8000. Regenerate these
# three lines with `tindahan-netlify-sync` when the tunnel host changes.
/api/*      https://concluded-boating-tahoe-lending.trycloudflare.com/api/:splat  200
/admin/*    https://concluded-boating-tahoe-lending.trycloudflare.com/admin/:splat  200
/static/*   https://concluded-boating-tahoe-lending.trycloudflare.com/static/:splat  200

# Everything else is the SPA (hash routing, so no deep-link rewrite needed).
/*  /index.html  200
